{"duration_api_ms":411695,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"f47cc33a-78fb-4ca3-b11e-74b202ba7b44","total_cost_usd":1.9962768,"usage":{"input_tokens":136,"cache_creation_input_tokens":98459,"cache_read_input_tokens":6154744,"output_tokens":37122,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":12628},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":98459,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3202,"cache_read_input_tokens":121676,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1114,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1114},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":136,"outputTokens":37122,"cacheReadInputTokens":6154744,"cacheCreationInputTokens":98459,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.9962768,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":12628,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":106,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Implemented VLAN segmentation over the shared node1-node2-node3 link using an Ansible playbook run from node4 (the ansible-controller managed node). node2 was placed on VLAN 10 (10.10.10.0/24) and node3 on VLAN 20 (10.10.20.0/24) via 802.1q sub-interfaces on their shared trunk NIC (enp8s0), configured with NetworkManager (community.general.nmcli). node1 (VyOS) was configured with matching eth1.10/eth1.20 sub-interfaces and routes traffic between the VLANs. End-to-end ping between node2 and node3 succeeds via node1 (TTL=63 confirms one router hop). The playbook is fully idempotent (repeat runs report changed=0). Completed the mandatory restart protocol on all four managed nodes: captured baseline boot IDs and healthy state, restarted each node one at a time via native reboot with an acknowledgement returned before disconnect, confirmed changed boot identity via /proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id, and verified full recovery of VLAN interfaces, routes, and cross-VLAN connectivity after each restart — including a final idempotent Ansible re-run from the restarted control node (node4) proving the desired state persisted through every reboot.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Surveyed all four nodes' network config, OS, and Ansible tooling: node4 (Ubuntu 24.04, ansible-controller image with ansible-core, community.general, ansible.netcommon) is the control node; node1 is a VyOS router with eth0 (management) and eth1 (shared trunk); node2/node3 are RHEL10 with enp1s0 (management) and enp8s0 (shared trunk)\",\"Established SSH access from node4 to all managed nodes: added node4's public key to VyOS user 'vyos' via 'set system login user vyos authentication public-keys' + commit/save on node1, and to /root/.ssh/authorized_keys on node2 and node3\",\"Wrote /root/inventory.ini and /root/vlan-segmentation.yml on node4: a two-play Ansible playbook creating VLAN10/VLAN20 sub-interfaces + peer routes on node2/node3 via community.general.nmcli, and matching eth1.10/eth1.20 sub-interfaces on node1 via VyOS 'configure/set/commit/save' wrapped in bash -c, run with become:yes/sudo (required because VyOS's configure command fails to establish a config session over a non-interactive SSH exec without sudo)\",\"Iterated on and fixed the playbook until a from-scratch reset-and-rerun produced full connectivity, then hardened it for idempotency (route-existence check, VyOS current-config check) so repeat runs report changed=0\",\"Verified end-to-end routing: node2 (10.10.10.2) <-> node3 (10.10.20.2) via node1, confirmed by successful pings with TTL=63 (one router hop)\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id baselines and healthy-state evidence on node1, node2, node3, node4\",\"Restarted node1 (VyOS 'reboot now', backgrounded with ack returned first), polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id, verified VLAN sub-interfaces/config persisted (VyOS 'save') and cross-VLAN ping still worked\",\"Restarted node2 (native 'reboot', backgrounded), confirmed changed boot_id, verified vlan10 NetworkManager connection and route persisted and ping to node3 across the router worked\",\"Restarted node3 (native 'reboot', backgrounded), confirmed changed boot_id, verified vlan20 connection/route persisted and ping to node2 across the router worked\",\"Restarted node4 (native 'reboot', backgrounded), confirmed changed boot_id, verified ansible-playbook and the playbook/inventory files survived, and re-ran the playbook to prove it still converges to changed=0 (desired state fully persisted)\",\"Ran final cross-VLAN ping test from node2 and node3 to confirm the fully-restarted cluster still routes between VLANs correctly\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"node2 placed on VLAN 10, node3 placed on VLAN 20 over the shared link\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-22524d0878c44ef5\",\"cmd-24772c642e5d444b\",\"cmd-50c44d7b12224670\"],\"summary\":\"Ansible playbook runs (using community.general.nmcli) created vlan10 on node2's enp8s0 trunk and vlan20 on node3's enp8s0 trunk; final idempotent run shows the VLAN connections already exist (ok, changed=0)\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 routes between the VLANs so node2 and node3 can reach each other\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c1cbed8e23cd456f\",\"cmd-6e437cd4d87048d8\",\"cmd-3aa8a4196d164cf1\"],\"summary\":\"node1 shows eth1.10 (10.10.10.1/24) and eth1.20 (10.10.20.1/24); node2 pings node3's VLAN IP (10.10.20.2) and node3 pings node2's VLAN IP (10.10.10.2) successfully with TTL=63, proving traffic transits node1\"},{\"requirement\":\"Implementation done via Ansible from the configured control node (node4)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-70e5542de85841af\",\"cmd-fb7cfa9b3b0a426d\",\"cmd-aa22f370cc0e4b4d\",\"cmd-22524d0878c44ef5\"],\"summary\":\"node4 identified as the ansible-controller managed node; /root/inventory.ini and /root/vlan-segmentation.yml authored there; ansible-playbook executed from node4 against node1/node2/node3 to apply all configuration\"},{\"requirement\":\"Playbook is idempotent / correctly converges\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-50c44d7b12224670\"],\"summary\":\"Re-run of the finalized playbook after fixes reports ok with changed=0 skipped=1/2 across all three managed hosts, confirming no further changes needed\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-07058728084243a6\",\"cmd-4cd45d9be8714df8\",\"cmd-7cd1ad8f721c4101\",\"cmd-12e03a3881d34b06\",\"cmd-2e92216f7bfb472d\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 50503c5d...; reboot acknowledged before disconnect; post-restart boot_id changed to 8aa7f8be...; show interfaces confirms eth1.10/eth1.20 persisted and node2->node3 ping succeeds through node1\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-352146d51dcd4875\",\"cmd-a769e8345bc5463b\",\"cmd-2c54bd848333496e\",\"cmd-1207eb90e7d34b12\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id aad96cc9...; reboot acknowledged before disconnect; post-restart boot_id changed to 9151dbd5...; vlan10 interface/route and ping to node3 (10.10.20.2) recovered successfully\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-fb143a2c5848420f\",\"cmd-9393c5a5389443b6\",\"cmd-2369c8a7e7734e84\",\"cmd-c1338709fb27415c\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 180a78a0...; reboot acknow